# Data conversion between gigabyte and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 1000MB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GB yields 1500.0MB; backward, converting 1MB to 0.001GB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 0.0015GB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
1000MB
1500.0MB
0.001GB
0.0015GB

<<< stderr
